jt-pve-storage-synology (0.5.5~beta1-1) unstable; urgency=high

  * 0.5.3~beta1 and 0.5.4~beta1 could not be used: pvesm add failed with
    "missing value for required option 'syno-password'" because PVE strips
    sensitive properties before validating required ones. Declared optional and
    enforced by the plugin.
  * CHAP was applied only when the target was created, so adding it to an
    existing storage gave no error and no access control. ensure now reconciles
    it, and the update hook pushes the secret to every target.
  * Refuse a CHAP username with no secret before writing anything.
  * Compute the effective config in the update hook: PVE applies deletions after
    the hook, so --delete of both CHAP options refused itself.

 -- Jason Cheng <jason@jason.tools>  Fri, 07 Aug 2026 00:30:00 +0800

jt-pve-storage-synology (0.5.4~beta1-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Fix CHAP, broken by 0.5.3~beta1's credential move: $scfg no longer carries
    the secret, and both consumers turned the missing value into an EMPTY CHAP
    secret rather than an error. Both now refuse.
  * Stop claiming the `copy` feature for a snapshot: path() dies on a snapname,
    so `qm clone --full --snapshot` failed partway instead of being refused.
  * Validate a snapshot's create_time instead of asserting its unit (R-25).

 -- Jason Cheng <jason@jason.tools>  Thu, 06 Aug 2026 23:00:00 +0800

jt-pve-storage-synology (0.5.3~beta1-1) unstable; urgency=high

  * SECURITY: the DSM credentials are no longer written to /etc/pve/storage.cfg,
    where they were readable by www-data and returned by the API to any user
    with Datastore.Audit. They now live in /etc/pve/priv/storage/<id>.syno.
    Run `pvesm set <storage> --syno-password <pw>` once per storage to migrate,
    and treat the old value as disclosed.
  * Release the DSM session in DESTROY: nine methods leaked one on their error
    paths.
  * Refuse a shrink instead of silently declining it.
  * Look a LUN name up before creating it, so the delete-on-refusal cleanup acts
    only on an object this call made.
  * Remove the credential file on every exit from on_delete_hook.

 -- Jason Cheng <jason@jason.tools>  Thu, 06 Aug 2026 21:00:00 +0800

