jt-pve-storage-synology (0.5.0~beta1-1) unstable; urgency=low

  * Verified on a two-node cluster: two DSM sessions on one account coexist,
    two iSCSI sessions on one target, offline migration in 2s and LIVE migration
    with 3ms downtime, data intact throughout.
  * find_multipaths is a per-node policy and decides whether a map exists at all.
    The plugin now makes the map exist with multipath -a <wwid> and fails the
    activation if it cannot, rather than returning a path to nothing.
  * debian/control describes what the package contains and depends on proxmox-ve,
    open-iscsi and multipath-tools.
  * Documented: removing a shared storage leaves other nodes' sessions behind,
    because on_delete_hook runs on one node only.

