jt-pve-storage-synology (0.4.1~beta1-1) unstable; urgency=low

  * A real VM booted from a Synology LUN, and a rollback was verified at the
    block level: pattern written, snapshotted, zeroed, rolled back, original
    sha256 returned.
  * qm destroy silently leaked its LUN every time: path() must return the OWNER
    as its second element, and returning the leaf name made PVE's check read
    "vm-9999-disk-0" != 9999 and skip vdisk_free entirely.
  * qm create with an existing volume died before starting: the base
    volume_size_info reaches filesystem_path. A sweep of the base class found
    five such methods; volume_export was refusing every disk move.
  * Host cache symmetry for snapshot and rollback, and an in-use check with its
    three-valued contract, verified against a booted VM.

 -- Jason Cheng (Jason Tools) <jason@jason.tools>  Fri, 07 Aug 2026 02:00:00 +0800

jt-pve-storage-synology (0.4.0~beta1-1) unstable; urgency=low

  * The plugin works: pvesm add synologysan registers, and add/alloc/activate/
    snapshot/rollback/clone/resize/free/remove have all been driven end to end
    against a DS918+ on DSM 7.1.1, twice, with no leftovers.
  * Five bugs found by running it rather than reading it: status() returns
    (total, available, used); pvesm alloc passes an empty name not undef; a
    resize must rescan the map's slaves; a LUN mapped to an existing session
    needs --rescan; and free_image and pvesm remove each left something behind.
  * A storage whose id folds onto another's LUN prefix on the same NAS is
    refused at add time.

 -- Jason Cheng (Jason Tools) <jason@jason.tools>  Fri, 07 Aug 2026 01:00:00 +0800

jt-pve-storage-synology (0.3.1~beta1-1) unstable; urgency=low

  * The PVE storage type is synologysan, not synologyiscsi. No type in this
    family carries a protocol in its name, and a type name cannot be renamed
    once anyone has used it — some Synology models support NVMe/TCP, at which
    point synologyiscsi would be a wrong name that could not be corrected.
    Changed now because the plugin is not written and it therefore costs nothing.
  * Synology::WwidState and Synology::Health.

 -- Jason Cheng (Jason Tools) <jason@jason.tools>  Fri, 07 Aug 2026 00:15:00 +0800

jt-pve-storage-synology (0.3.0~beta1-1) unstable; urgency=low

  * Synology::ISCSI, which never uses iscsiadm discovery: that creates node
    records for every target on the NAS, including ones already in use.
  * Read the per-model ceilings from the NAS: a DS918+ reports 256 LUNs and 128
    targets where the datasheet says 512 and 256. Refuse a create before the NAS
    does, with a message that names the reason.
  * make check-zh had no use utf8, so it passed on 62 real artefacts; then its
    code-span handling manufactured findings. Both fixed, all 62 corrected.

